 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20stop=20dispatching=20a=20competing=20run?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four data jobs pushed to main (which triggers deploy-pages via `on: push`)
and then ALSO ran `gh workflow run deploy-pages.yml`. Both runs landed in
`concurrency: pages, cancel-in-progress: true`, so one was cancelled — and
daily-price-refresh resolved its wait target with `gh run list --limit 1`,
which could hand it the cancelled run or the previous deploy. That is where
the 'may have been cancelled by a later push' failures come from.

- champions-replica-scrape, per-decklist-scrape, weekly-full-update: dispatch
  step removed. The push already deploys.
- daily-price-refresh keeps its wait — it exists so Telegram never alerts a
  price the origin has not published yet (2026-06 bug) — but now FINDS the
  run instead of creating one: the commit step exports the pushed sha and the
  next step polls deploy-pages runs for a matching headSha, with a 60 s window
  and the same fixed-sleep fallback as before.
- champions-replica-scrape drops `actions: write`; nothing dispatches now.

